error[E0409]: `+=` cannot join `str` and `{integer}`
 --> mem:///main.lu:3:10
  |
3 |     s += 1
  |          ^ this is `{integer}`
  |
  = note: `+=` joins a `str` with a `str` or a `char` (D62). Spell any other conversion inside an
    interpolation hole: `t += "{count}"` formats any primitive.
  = note: each `+` builds a fresh `str` — interpolation's cost model; `std.strbuf` is the builder
    for heavy loops.
